<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding area of a kite given diagonals</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A kite has diagonals measuring <b>{@d1@} cm</b> and <b>{@d2@} cm</b>.</p>
<p>Find its area.</p>

[[jsxgraph width="400px" height="400px"]]
    var d1 = {#d1#};
    var d2 = {#d2#};
    
    // Dynamically calculate tight boundaries based on the generated diagonals
    var max_x = d2/2 + 1.5;
    var max_y = d1/2 + 1.5;
    
    var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(BOARDID, {
        boundingbox: [-max_x, max_y, max_x, -max_y],
        maxboundingbox: [-max_x - 1, max_y + 1, max_x + 1, -max_y - 1],
        keepAspectRatio: true,
        axis: false,
        showCopyright: false,
        showNavigation: true 
    });

    // Define the vertices of the kite based on diagonals
    var top = board.create('point', [0, d1/2], {name: '', visible: false});
    var bottom = board.create('point', [0, -d1/2], {name: '', visible: false});
    var left = board.create('point', [-d2/2, 0], {name: '', visible: false});
    var right = board.create('point', [d2/2, 0], {name: '', visible: false});

    // Draw the Kite using original color scheme
    board.create('polygon', [top, right, bottom, left], {
        fillColor: 'none', 
        strokeColor: 'black', 
        strokeWidth: 2
    });

    // Draw the dashed diagonal lines
    board.create('segment', [top, bottom], {dash: 2, strokeColor: 'gray'});
    board.create('segment', [left, right], {dash: 2, strokeColor: 'gray'});

    // Clean dynamic labels anchored to the diagonals
    board.create('text', [0.2, d1/4, d1 + ' cm'], {anchorX: 'left', anchorY: 'middle', fontSize: 14});
    board.create('text', [d2/4, -0.3, d2 + ' cm'], {anchorX: 'middle', anchorY: 'top', fontSize: 14});
[[/jsxgraph]]

<p>Area = [[input:ans1]] <b>\(\text{cm}^2\)</b> [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>To find the area of a kite, we use the formula involving the lengths of its diagonals \(d_1\) and \(d_2\):</p>

<p>
\[ \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times d_1 \times d_2 \]
</p>

<p>Substituting the given values:</p>

<p>
\[ \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times {@d1@} \times {@d2@} \]
</p>
<p>
\[ \text{Area} = {@ta_float@} \text{ cm}^2 \]
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
